From b49abe942216196ceff0e8d5899fca7f8b7581ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 09:46:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 38/42] ui: rename customer label to namespace (display-only)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the multi-tenant context, the governance "customer" entity is more
accurately framed as a namespace within a tenant: a grouping of teams,
budgets, and rate limits. Flip user-facing labels (JSX text, dialog
titles, form labels, placeholders, toasts, aria-labels, sidebar nav,
empty-state copy) from Customer/Customers to Namespace/Namespaces.

Code identifiers, API paths, type names, Redux tags, URL routes,
RBAC resource names, and prop names are unchanged — this is purely a
copy refresh. Unrelated "customer support" placeholder text in prompt
sheets is left as-is.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
